  "book": "A single volume, the first part (pars prior) of Casaubon's De quatuor linguis commentatio (London, 1650). It runs from front matter (preface, errata) through De lingua Hebraica and De lingua Anglica vetere sive Saxonica, which holds a Greek-letter lexicon of Saxon words, the closing sections and a Saxon alphabet. Then come the Addenda, Somner's glossary of Old German words, and an index.",
